<urn:usf:capability-implementation-convention:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:antiSelfWarrant> "The implementation unit and the conformance unit are separate semantic work units, dispatched independently and routed to different models whenever more than one eligible route exists. An implementation therefore does not author the evidence that satisfies it, and the facet evaluator reads the executed outcome rather than any assertion made by the producing unit." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:capability-implementation-convention:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:authoredVersusGenerated> "Capability modules and their conformance tests are model-authored under graph-derived paths and graph-derived semantics. They are classified as generated-under-authority rather than hand-authored, and no model contributes a path, filename or module boundary." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:capability-implementation-convention:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "v1" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:capability-implementation-convention:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:cohesionRule> "Every outstanding applicable implementation-conformance facet of one capability describes the behaviour of that capability's single module, so those facets form exactly one implementation work unit. A facet boundary is a requirement boundary, not a work boundary, and one facet per prompt is prohibited." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:capability-implementation-convention:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:conformancePathRule> <urn:usf:delivery-path-rule:capabilityconformance> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:capability-implementation-convention:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:dependencyDerivationRule> "Exactly one implementation dependency edge exists per capability: the conformance unit requires the concrete implementation module, because a behavioural test cannot be written against a module whose exported surface does not yet exist. No capability implementation depends on another capability implementation: the contracts and facet statements already carry the authority each module needs, so the ready frontier is every capability with outstanding work." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:capability-implementation-convention:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:filenameConvention> "One module per capability named exactly the capability canonicalName with a .ts extension, under a directory named for the capability's domain. The conformance test carries the same stem with a .conformance.test.ts extension. No other filename is authorized and no additional file may be created by a work unit." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:capability-implementation-convention:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:implementationPathRule> <urn:usf:delivery-path-rule:capabilityimplementation> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:capability-implementation-convention:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "A module realized at its canonical path is not evidence of conformance. Only an executed behavioural outcome recorded under the implementation-conformance rule can evidence an implementation-conformance facet." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:capability-implementation-convention:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "This convention states where capability implementation code belongs and how work is decomposed. It asserts nothing about whether any capability is implemented, and it is not evidence for any facet." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:capability-implementation-convention:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:outputRule> "A capability module is a self-contained TypeScript module with no runtime dependency outside the Node standard library and its own capability directory. It exports named pure functions and the declared state and error identifiers its facets require, so the behaviour every facet statement asserts is directly invocable from a test." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:capability-implementation-convention:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:ownedByRepository> <urn:usf:delivery-repository:usf-platform> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:capability-implementation-convention:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:pathDerivation> "canonicalPath = the owning repository realisationRoot joined with the governing pathPattern, in which {domain} is the local name of the capability inDomain object and {capability} is the capability canonicalName. Both substitutions come from the graph, so a model never proposes, chooses or influences a path." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:capability-implementation-convention:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CapabilityImplementationConvention> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
