<urn:usf:core-surface-policy:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "A profile-supplied requirement is excluded from Core's completion denominator because it is not Core's to satisfy. It is not evidence that any profile has satisfied it." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:core-surface-policy:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Marking a requirement profile-supplied does not retract the recovered V1 applicability that recorded it. V1 USF satisfied these requirements; V3 Core deliberately does not, and the requirement passes to whichever profile needs it rather than ceasing to exist." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:core-surface-policy:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:ownerAuthorityRule> "A user interface belongs to the product. A profile that needs one declares its own UI semantics against the Core grammar, and may need surfaces Core has no equivalent for. Core supplies the grammar for describing a UI; it declares no surface of its own." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:core-surface-policy:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:surfaceRule> "Every USF Core capability must be fully usable through an SDK surface, an API surface and a CLI surface. A capability reachable only through a rendered interface is incomplete as Core, because a product cannot compose what it cannot call." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:core-surface-policy:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:CoreSurfacePolicy> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
