<urn:usf:delivery-facet:abacpolicydecisionpointlifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The decision point reads the current resource policy, audits, and sets a replacement, while request evaluation is authorization-server-first when a token is present, falls back to a static permission backstop when the resource is unregistered or the server is unavailable, denies fail-closed on policy denial, and requests step-up on insufficient auth level. Policy administration and per-request evaluation are distinct flows over the same guard metadata." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
