<urn:usf:delivery-facet:accessibilitya11ygatepermissions> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The a11y gate owns no tenant data and exposes no tenant-mutating routes, so standard platform security controls apply; the gate is an operator/CI concern rather than an end-user permission. Accessibility expectations apply to UI surfaces for all users and are not tenant-gated. Configuring exceptions is a governance authority, not an end-user role." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
