<urn:usf:delivery-facet:accessibilitya11ygatestatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The state is the set of accessibility expectations and the latest gate results rather than owned tenant rows: the required landmarks, roles, ARIA attributes, and axe rule outcomes per audited surface, held as configuration and evidence. It has no owned database schema, so backup scope is configuration/evidence only and restore cannot create tenant data. Results are per-run evidence reconciled against the expected accessibility contract." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
