<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformauditmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetKind> <urn:usf:facet-kind:auditmodel> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformauditmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Login and session creation are represented by authentication events and session-store state, and logout removes session state, while read-only session lookup and discovery validation carry no mutation audit. Every administrative mutation (provider create/update/delete/test, MFA, lockout, session, and claim-mapping changes) emits an audit-before-change event recording alias, operation, changed field names, and secret-changed booleans only; configuration and secret values are never audited, and audit failure aborts the mutation before the provider is touched." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
