<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformerrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "authenticationplatformerrormodel" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformerrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetApplicability> "APPLICABLE" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformerrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetKind> <urn:usf:facet-kind:errormodel> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformerrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "All failures are fail-closed: an unauthenticated session lookup returns an unauthenticated/401 result, callback failures redirect to the login page with a generic sign-in error, and session-store lookup failure falls through to unauthenticated without leaking provider detail. Administrative failures map to typed outcomes such as validation error, no-tenant, no-credential, invalid-credential, forbidden-realm-operation, realm-unreachable, not-found, issuer-mismatch, JWKS-invalid, unreachable, and invalid-document; provider failure returns a typed degraded/readiness result, keeps mutation boundaries closed, and never fabricates successful provider state, and inactive or unknown custom hosts degrade to the platform realm rather than being trusted." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformerrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementClass> "behavioural-runtime" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
