<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformlifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetApplicability> "APPLICABLE" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformlifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetKind> <urn:usf:facet-kind:lifecycle> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformlifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Spans the full platform sign-in surface: login initiates a PKCE/state/nonce redirect handoff, the callback validates state/code/nonce and resolves identity into a server-side session, session reads return authenticated or unauthenticated context, and logout idempotently destroys session and clears host-only plus domain-scoped cookies. It also covers IdP and policy administration lifecycles (list/create/update/rotate-secret/enable/disable/delete identity providers, OIDC discovery import, and read/validate/write of MFA, lockout, session, and claim-mapping policy). Each administrative mutation resolves the tenant credential, audits, then writes to the identity provider and may be read back." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformlifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementClass> "behavioural-runtime" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
