<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformpermissions> <urn:usf:predicate:facetApplicability> "APPLICABLE" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformpermissions> <urn:usf:predicate:facetKind> <urn:usf:facet-kind:permissions> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformpermissions> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The login/session path establishes the actor rather than requiring a permission, converting resolved roles into an explicit permission bundle where tenant roles come from membership and system-admin comes from realm roles without tenant membership. All authentication-administration routes are tenant-scoped and require read or write auth-settings permission with the matching admin scope, resolving the tenant credential from the FQDN-derived tenant context so one tenant can never read or mutate another tenant's provider, policy, or mapping configuration. Custom-domain callback eligibility is gated by tenant domain-write lifecycle operations." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
