<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformreadinessmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetApplicability> "APPLICABLE" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformreadinessmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetKind> <urn:usf:facet-kind:readinessmodel> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformreadinessmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Readiness for the live session path depends on identity-provider, session-store, and configuration availability, with an explicit deterministic fixture mode for tests; administrative readiness is credential-derived and only reports configured/ok when the tenant realm credential can read and mutate policies, otherwise classifying missing-credential, invalid-credential, forbidden-realm-operation, realm-unreachable, or discovery-invalid rather than hiding them. Degraded mode disables provider-dependent mutation paths while keeping read-only readiness and audit visible, and real brokered/interactive IdP login is carried as externally limited rather than fake-passed." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
