<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformstatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetKind> <urn:usf:facet-kind:statemodel> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformstatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Authentication state moves unauthenticated -> authenticating -> authenticated or denied, materialised as a session record carrying session id, user id, tenant and organisation id, roles, resolved permission bundle, display name, and expiry, with no-membership and system-admin sessions holding empty tenant context by design. Administrative state includes per-tenant identity-provider definitions (alias, enabled, masked secret, scopes, issuer/JWKS validation result), OIDC discovery validation states, MFA mode (none/optional/required with TOTP or WebAuthn), lockout thresholds, and session lifespan policy. Custom-domain callback derivation depends on a domain's verified-and-active state, falling back to the platform realm for inactive or unknown hosts." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
