<urn:usf:delivery-facet:authenticationplatformvalidation> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Login sanitises the return-to target, emits PKCE challenge parameters, binds the callback to the pre-auth cookie, and rejects missing or unknown state/code and provider error callbacks while accepting only stored session cookies. Administrative validation enforces provider allowlists, required and safe-scheme OIDC URLs, reserved-alias rules, discovery issuer and JWKS validity (allowing plain HTTP only for local hosts), MFA enum values, positive lockout thresholds, bounded session lifespans, non-dangerous claim names, and realm roles restricted to the tenant-role allowlist; secrets are preserved when omitted on update and invalid bodies stop before any audit or provider mutation." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
