<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backgroundworkersjobrunnerauditmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Heartbeats are operational telemetry and are not audit events; the auditable actions in this domain (operator redrive and related operations) are emitted by the event capability rather than by the worker. This keeps the worker's high-frequency liveness signal out of the privileged-action audit trail while still leaving redrive and operator actions auditable upstream." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
