<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backgroundworkersjobrunnererrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Outcomes are deterministic and fail closed: a handler error becomes a retry or, at maxAttempts, a dead-letter; an unavailable Postgres substrate causes an honest proof skip or readiness failure; and stale or stopped workers are explicit liveness states rather than hidden errors. Degraded mode disables the processing paths that depend on the Postgres adapter while keeping read-only readiness visible, and no path fabricates a processed result." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
