<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backgroundworkersjobrunnerlifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "A worker emits a heartbeat to mark itself alive, claims a pending event from the event substrate, runs its registered handler, marks the event processed, idempotently skips events already processed, retries a failing handler, dead-letters the event once maxAttempts is reached, and exposes its liveness. The runner consumes the durable-queue records produced by the event bus and applies retry, dead-letter, and redrive-compatible semantics so deferred work executes exactly-effectively once. Provider failure degrades readiness and keeps mutation boundaries closed rather than processing unsafely." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backgroundworkersjobrunnerlifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementClass> "behavioural-runtime" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
