<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backgroundworkersjobrunnerreadinessmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Readiness is worker heartbeat liveness (alive|stale|stopped) together with the event-processing proof; a failure to claim, process, or dead-letter is a proof and readiness failure rather than a silent stall. Readiness degrades explicitly when the substrate is unavailable and never upgrades a production-shaped state to production-live. Liveness states are surfaced rather than masked so stale or stopped workers are visible to operators." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
