<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backgroundworkersjobrunnerstatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "State comprises workerId, workerKind, a heartbeat timestamp, liveness in alive|stale|stopped, the status of the claimed event, a retry count, and the dead-letter transition; the runner does not own tenant records and reads pending and dead-letter queues from the event-bus state model. Idempotency is anchored on the event's processed status so a re-delivered or reclaimed event is not processed twice. Liveness is derived from heartbeat age rather than stored as a separate authoritative flag." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
