<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backgroundworkersjobrunnervalidation> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Worker processing only claims pending events, never reclaims an already-processed event, honours maxAttempts before dead-lettering, and records a heartbeat for the supplied worker id and kind. Idempotent skip of processed events is the core invariant that prevents duplicate side effects under retry or redelivery. These behaviours are exercised by the event-worker runtime proof." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
