<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backupandrestoreauditmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Backup artifacts are written with owner-only permissions to a controlled, git-ignored location so dumps are not inadvertently exposed or committed. Operator actions are environment-gated and explicit, leaving the override or confirmation token as the human-attributable signal that a destructive operation was deliberately authorised. Promotion and readiness proof logs record that the backup proof executed." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
