<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backupandrestorecontracts> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The contract is a pair of operations: produce a timestamped compressed dump of the canonical database, and restore a named compressed dump over a target database, each subject to its environment guard. Backup owns no tenant data and restore cannot fabricate tenant data; for higher environments disaster recovery uses a stage-equivalent managed snapshot rather than these local scripts. These scripts already encode the destructive-operation controls the platform requires and are intended to be reused unchanged." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
