<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backupandrestoreerrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The operations fail closed: a missing or non-matching environment override or confirmation token aborts before any destructive action, and a script failure leaves the target database untouched rather than partially applied. There is no owned tenant data, so the dominant risk is semantic drift or configuration loss rather than tenant-row loss; provider (dump/restore tooling) failure surfaces a typed degraded or readiness failure without fabricating success." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backupandrestoreerrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementClass> "behavioural-runtime" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
