<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backupandrestorelifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:admissibleEvidenceClass> "realized-artefact" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backupandrestorelifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "backupandrestorelifecycle" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backupandrestorelifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetApplicability> "APPLICABLE" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backupandrestorelifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetKind> <urn:usf:facet-kind:lifecycle> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backupandrestorelifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Backup and restore are operational scripts, not an owned schema: backup dumps the canonical relational database and compresses it to an owner-only, version-control-ignored local artifact, while restore destructively overwrites a target database from such an archive. Scope is the canonical relational store only; rebuildable cache, the analytical mirror, and object storage have no platform backup script because they are not canonical state and recover via provider-native lifecycle. The capability owns no tenant records, so its backup scope is configuration and evidence and a restore cannot itself create tenant data." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backupandrestorelifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementClass> "artefact-content" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
