<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backupandrestorepermissions> <urn:usf:predicate:facetKind> <urn:usf:facet-kind:permissions> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backupandrestorepermissions> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Both operations are guarded environment-gated operator actions. Backup refuses to run outside development or test environments unless an explicit allow-environment override names the target, so a shared database is never quietly dumped. Restore refuses unless the environment is development or test AND a confirmation token matching the exact environment is supplied, making the destructive overwrite intentionally hard to trigger by accident." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
