<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backupandrestorereadinessmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Readiness reflects whether the backup path can produce a valid artifact in the current environment under its guard; when the dump or restore tooling is unavailable the capability degrades, disabling the destructive path while keeping read-only readiness visible. Readiness being blocked, a failed backup proof during promotion, or repeated typed errors over threshold raise alerts. Restore is never part of normal readiness flow because it is destructive and confirmation-gated." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
