<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backupandrestorestatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetKind> <urn:usf:facet-kind:statemodel> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:backupandrestorestatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "There is no owned database schema; the durable artifact is the compressed dump file written with a restrictive umask and owner-only file permissions to a git-ignored local artifacts location. Restore consumes one such archive and replaces the target database wholesale. Recovery posture for non-canonical stores is explicit: cache is rebuildable, the analytical store is a mirror, and object data is provider-managed, so none participate in this script's state." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
