<urn:usf:delivery-facet:brandingandtheminglifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Branding resolves from a default theme overlaid by tenant theme overrides into an effective theme response used to bootstrap the client shell, while richer branding edits (such as application name and theme selection) flow through the configuration registry as managed override definitions. The lifecycle therefore spans an unauthenticated bootstrap read and audited, permissioned branding mutations through the configuration plane." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
