<urn:usf:delivery-facet:brandingandthemingpermissions> <urn:usf:predicate:facetKind> <urn:usf:facet-kind:permissions> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:brandingandthemingpermissions> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The theme bootstrap read is unauthenticated and host-derived so the client shell can style itself before login, whereas registry-based branding edits require tenant-scoped configuration read/write permissions with per-definition permission enforcement. Branding overrides are tenant-isolated through the same configuration plane, so a tenant only ever reads or writes its own branding values." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
