<urn:usf:delivery-facet:configurationregistryandhistoryauditmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "A set operation emits the definition's configured change audit action and a clear operation emits a value-cleared audit action, in both cases before the tenant settings are mutated and carrying key and value metadata. Audit emission is a precondition for the write, so a failed audit prevents the persistence change entirely." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
