<urn:usf:delivery-facet:configurationregistryandhistorylifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "A configuration definition moves through active, deprecated, and internal states, and the runtime resolves an effective value per tenant from either the platform default or a tenant override. Setting an override performs an audit-first upsert and clearing it performs an audit-first delete, after which a best-effort change-notification event is emitted; the audit precedes the persistence mutation so the change is always recorded." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
