<urn:usf:delivery-facet:environmentregistryandbootstraperrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Provider failure returns a typed degraded/readiness failure, keeps mutation boundaries closed, and does not fabricate successful provider state; degraded mode disables side-effect paths that depend on the manifest-env adapter while keeping read-only readiness and audit visible. The risk class is semantic drift or configuration loss, not tenant data loss. A failed bootstrap or blocked readiness is an alertable provider-dependency condition." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
