<urn:usf:delivery-facet:environmentspecificvssharedservicemodellifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Classification model that decides whether each service is environment-specific or shared and governs the routing and isolation that follows; it is provider-backed but owns no database schema. It deploys a classification contract (V1 contract n/a) and must keep its lifecycle/readiness model unchanged during extraction, with migrations limited to contract/config references that must update semantic artefacts when behaviour changes. Rollback restores the previous classification implementation and re-runs the named proof evidence." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
