<urn:usf:delivery-facet:eventbusdurablequeuesdlqredrivelifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The capability publishes a pending event, deduplicates it by organisation, event type, and caller-supplied idempotency key, lets a worker claim and process it to processed, retries a failing handler with bounded backoff up to maxAttempts, then transitions the record to dead_letter; an operator redrive re-enqueues a dead-lettered event as a fresh pending event under a new idempotency key. Canonical product events carry strict, versioned payload contracts (for example tenant.config.changed keyed on key and report.run keyed on reportId) while the generic event-bus path also backs test-only fixture events excluded from product readiness. Provider failure degrades readiness rather than fabricating successful delivery." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
