<urn:usf:delivery-facet:eventbusdurablequeuesdlqredrivepermissions> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Routes are global, operator-only platform surfaces: reading the event list and the dead-letter list requires platform.events.read, redrive requires platform.events.write, and worker listing requires platform.workers.read. Tenant isolation is enforced by organisationId partitioning plus row-level security so one organisation can never observe or redrive another organisation's events, and list routes require an explicit organisationId. Secrets and provider credentials never cross the event boundary." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
