<urn:usf:delivery-facet:eventbusdurablequeuesdlqredrivereadinessmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Readiness combines operator visibility of the event and dead-letter queues with worker heartbeat liveness (alive|stale|stopped); it degrades explicitly and disables mutation/side-effect paths that depend on the Postgres adapter while keeping read-only readiness and audit visible. Live proofs fail closed on row-level-security, secret-payload, retry, redrive, or heartbeat regressions and skip honestly when Postgres is unavailable, so production-shaped readiness is never reported as production-live." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
