<urn:usf:delivery-facet:eventbusdurablequeuesdlqredrivestatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Persistent state is the platform_events table partitioned by organisationId, holding eventType, idempotencyKey, payload, status in pending|processing|processed|dead_letter, and attempts against maxAttempts, alongside worker_heartbeats recording alive|stale|stopped liveness. Dead-letter records retain tenant, event type, attempt count, a payload summary, and the last error so redrive can reconstruct context; ordering is guaranteed per organisation and idempotency key with no cross-tenant ordering guarantee. Row-level security scopes every read and mutation to the owning organisation." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
