<urn:usf:delivery-facet:historyreadmodelreadonlyprojectionerrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Because it is read-only there is no mutation to roll back; failures return a typed degraded or readiness error rather than a partial or fabricated result, and the read fails closed when tenant context or the substrate is unavailable. Provider failure keeps boundaries closed and does not invent history entries. Tenant data cannot be exposed across tenants." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
