<urn:usf:delivery-facet:historyreadmodelreadonlyprojectionpermissions> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Reads are tenant-scoped so a tenant sees only its own history, while the admin variant is operator-scoped to read a named tenant's history under privileged access; both preserve tenant isolation. Because the projection omits payloads, tokens, and secrets, even authorised readers cannot extract sensitive material through history. Access flows through ports and adapters, never a direct client database connection." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
