<urn:usf:delivery-facet:historyreadmodelreadonlyprojectionstatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Each history entry carries an identifier, source, type, title, occurrence time, and a safe actor/status summary, returned with total, limit, and offset for paging; it deliberately excludes raw metadata, payloads, tokens, and secrets. The model is a projection over existing audit and event records rather than an owned canonical table, served through a history repository port. Paging fields make the read-only result set bounded and navigable." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
