<urn:usf:delivery-facet:i18nruntimeandvalidationcontracts> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The contract has two faces: the runtime locale-resolution interface that resolves keys to strings for a locale, and the validation interface that asserts required keys exist, no raw literals leak, and interpolation parameters match. Configuration is read from the declared provider/config plane and missing or invalid configuration fails closed instead of inventing defaults. UI strings are contractual, so missing keys are a contract violation rather than a soft fallback." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
