<urn:usf:delivery-facet:logsaggregationandtenantscopedsearchreadinessmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Readiness is a first-class, queryable posture reporting the discrete sub-states (log ingestion, tenant-scoped query, trace correlation, dashboards, collector, metrics, error capture) and degrades explicitly when the search adapter or substrate is unavailable. In degraded mode mutation/side-effect paths that depend on the search adapter are disabled while read-only readiness and audit visibility are retained; emitted readiness, error, and audit signals use the controlled, OpenTelemetry-informed observability vocabulary." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
