<urn:usf:delivery-facet:logsaggregationandtenantscopedsearchstatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Persisted state is log entries keyed by low-cardinality service and level labels, with high-cardinality identifiers (organisation/tenant id, request id, trace id) carried as structured fields rather than labels to control series cardinality. Backing the entries is a readiness record exposing the discrete states log ingestion, tenant-scoped query, trace correlation, dashboards, collector, metrics, and error capture; schema evolution uses ordered, forward-only migrations that preserve tenant rows and audit lineage." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
