<urn:usf:delivery-facet:metricsandtraceserrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Provider failure returns a typed degraded/readiness failure and never fabricates successful provider state; repeated typed errors crossing a threshold are an explicit alert condition. Because the capability owns no tenant data, the dominant failure risk is semantic drift or configuration loss rather than data loss, and error paths keep mutation boundaries closed." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
