<urn:usf:delivery-facet:notificationdeliveryandpreferencesandchannelslifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The lifecycle is: a user sets channel and category preferences, a test or domain notification is dispatched, disabled channels are suppressed, enabled channels are delivered through the local, email, or webhook transport, each attempt is logged as sent|suppressed|failed, and channel readiness is reported. Notifications are requested by workflow and other producer events only after preference and channel checks pass, and a missing recipient fails rather than being faked as sent. Transport-provider failure degrades readiness and never marks an undelivered notification as delivered." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
