<urn:usf:delivery-facet:notificationdeliveryandpreferencesandchannelsreadinessmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Readiness reports the real availability of the local, SMTP, and webhook transports; the Mailpit and webhook proofs skip honestly when their backing services are absent and never mark a fake send as sent. Because this is a tenant-data capability, readiness must also preserve tenant isolation and audit signals, and a missing isolation or audit signal is an alert condition. Provider failure degrades readiness explicitly rather than upgrading a composed or production-shaped state to production-live." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
