<urn:usf:delivery-facet:notificationdeliveryandpreferencesandchannelsvalidation> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Invalid profile or preference bodies are rejected, an invalid tenant id is rejected, secret-bearing notification payloads are rejected before dispatch, disabled preferences suppress delivery, and a missing recipient fails rather than reporting a fake send. These invariants are exercised by the notification preference, dispatch, and transport runtime proofs so suppression and failure are explicit states, not silent drops." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
