<urn:usf:delivery-facet:objectstorageandtenantprefixesandsignedurlsauditmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Object lifecycle transitions (upload, scan outcome, quarantine, rejection) are recorded in the tenant-scoped registry, and operations preserve tenant context through spans with typed logs carrying the tenant/organisation identifier. Signed-URL issuance is bounded and attributable, and recovery must preserve tenant boundary, audit, and data-subject evidence. Quota changes are observable through the storage-bytes meter." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
