<urn:usf:delivery-facet:objectstorageandtenantprefixesandsignedurlserrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The model is fail-closed and security-sensitive: an unscanned or quarantined object is not served as clean, provider failure returns a typed degraded or readiness error with mutation boundaries closed, and the capability never fabricates a successful upload or a valid signed URL. Tenant data cannot be silently dropped or remapped, and cross-tenant access is denied by prefix and registry isolation. Incident class is tenant-data-or-security." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
