<urn:usf:delivery-facet:objectstorageandtenantprefixesandsignedurlspermissions> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Objects are isolated by tenant prefix and by tenant-scoped registry access, so one tenant cannot enumerate or read another tenant's objects, and access to bytes is mediated by short-lived signed URLs rather than open buckets. The provider is identity-integrated so claim-to-policy mapping governs bucket access, and tenant-scoped registry rows enforce isolation in the database layer. Object operations are security-sensitive and must preserve permission and isolation." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
