<urn:usf:delivery-facet:objectstorageandtenantprefixesandsignedurlsstatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Each object is represented by a registry record carrying an object id, tenant/organisation id, object key, content type, size in bytes, scan state (uploaded, quarantined, clean, or rejected), timestamps, and the tenant prefix, with storage usage tracked against a storage-bytes quota meter. Object bytes are held under a tenant-scoped key prefix in the object-storage provider, while the registry row is the relational source of truth for lifecycle and quota. The registry table is tenant-scoped under row-level security." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
