<urn:usf:delivery-facet:pitrretentionlegalholddataresidencylifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Provides point-in-time recovery drills, per-resource retention windows, legal holds that block deletion, and single-region data-residency tagging over tenant data, exposed through administrative data operations. A retention worker periodically evaluates expired candidates and deletes or anonymises them UNLESS an active legal hold protects the resource; legal holds move from active to released and residency tags are owned on the tenant record. The whole capability fails closed where source data or configuration is unavailable so that retention never destroys protected or unverified data." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
