<urn:usf:delivery-facet:productcatalogplanspricesstatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "State is a three-level hierarchy: Product (identifier, name, description, active flag, created timestamp), Plan (identifier, owning product, name, currency, billing period, active flag, created timestamp), and Price (identifier, owning plan, version, price type, unit amount, currency, billing period, active flag, created timestamp). Items carry explicit active/inactive state rather than being hard-deleted, and price versioning preserves historical amounts. State changes flow through ordered migrations that must preserve this proven model." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
