<urn:usf:delivery-facet:providerconfigurationplanecontracts> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The interface contract is the provider-config repository behind a port (provider-config-repository) plus the admin create/read, lifecycle-transition, and delete operations. Configuration is read from the declared provider/config plane and missing or invalid configuration fails closed rather than inventing defaults. The lifecycleState transitions are the contractual states consumers depend on to know whether a provider is usable." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
