<urn:usf:delivery-facet:providerconfigurationplanelifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Manages provider configurations through an explicit lifecycle (proposed, configured, ready, degraded, disabled) so each provider instance is declared, validated, and promoted deliberately; it is provider-backed and database-backed but owns no tenant records. It deploys the V1-proven contract for GET/POST /api/admin/provider-configs plus the per-id lifecycle and delete operations and must keep its lifecycle/readiness model unchanged during extraction. Recovery re-runs proof:provider-config and proof:provider-readiness-contract before promotion continues." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
