<urn:usf:delivery-facet:providerconfigurationplanereadinessmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Readiness is encoded directly in lifecycleState: a provider is ready only after it is configured, credentialed where required, and health-probed, and it degrades explicitly when the probe or substrate is unavailable. Readiness fails closed and stays visible read-only in degraded mode. Promotion is gated on proof:provider-config and proof:provider-readiness-contract passing." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
