<urn:usf:delivery-facet:providerconfigurationplanestatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "State includes providerKey, capability, environment, instanceLabel, classification, lifecycleState (proposed, configured, ready, degraded, disabled), endpoint, config, credentialRef, requiresCredential, and audit metadata. Database changes use ordered SQL migrations that must preserve this proven state model, and rollback is forward-fix or guarded restore after migration lineage is verified. Credentials are referenced rather than embedded, keeping secret material out of the configuration record." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
