<urn:usf:delivery-facet:providerenvironmentclassificationpermissions> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "It owns no tenant records and exposes no tenant-mutating routes, so standard platform security controls apply; its tenant impact is indirect through correct posture labelling. Classification is an operator/governance concern, not an end-user permission. The separation it enforces is what prevents a hermetic or sandbox provider from being treated as production-live." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
