<urn:usf:delivery-facet:relationalstorageandmigrationsandrlsauditmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "State-changing access preserves tenant context through route, use-case, and provider spans, and typed error logs carry the tenant/organisation identifier when the operation is tenant-scoped. The migration ledger is itself an audit trail: each applied file is recorded with its checksum and timestamp, and historical files retain their decision-reference comment blocks so that later forward corrections remain traceable to the file they supersede. Recovery and restore must preserve tenant boundary, audit, and data-subject evidence." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
