<urn:usf:delivery-facet:relationalstorageandmigrationsandrlscontracts> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "No client connects directly to the store; all data access is mediated through repository ports and adapters per the hexagonal constraint, with each bounded context exposing typed repository operations. The migration contract is forward-only with one transaction per file, code-point apply ordering, and a single secret-materialisation trust boundary that substitutes only the managed application-role password placeholder after rejecting quote, backslash, and control characters. New tenant-scoped tables MUST attach the canonical RLS predicate and the FORCE row-level-security setting as a contract obligation." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
