<urn:usf:delivery-facet:relationalstorageandmigrationsandrlserrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetKind> <urn:usf:facet-kind:errormodel> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:relationalstorageandmigrationsandrlserrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Failures are deterministic and fail-closed: a checksum mismatch or a failing migration aborts the run, rolls back that file's transaction, and records nothing, so the operator fixes forward and re-runs safely. Missing or invalid configuration fails closed rather than inventing defaults, and provider failure returns a typed degraded or readiness error while keeping mutation boundaries closed and never fabricating successful provider state. Tenant data is never silently dropped or remapped; rollback is forward-fix or a guarded restore only after migration lineage is verified." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
