<urn:usf:delivery-facet:relationalstorageandmigrationsandrlslifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Governs the canonical relational store as a forward-only, numbered migration chain applied by a deterministic runner inside one transaction per file, recording each applied file with its content checksum so already-applied files become effectively immutable and corrections ship only as new forward migrations (never edits). Fresh installs apply the full chain in code-point order; an existing install skips checksum-matched files and applies only the new tail, so an existing install is already a current install at the data layer with zero data movement for prior files. The runner refuses to proceed on any checksum mismatch for an applied file, making the chain the load-bearing provenance and the data-verification gate." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
