<urn:usf:delivery-facet:relationalstorageandmigrationsandrlspermissions> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The runtime application connects as a non-superuser role that is explicitly NOINHERIT and does not bypass row-level security, so tenant isolation is enforced for normal traffic; privileged operations switch transaction-locally to a dedicated bypass role. The canonical RLS predicate admits a row only when its tenant identifier equals the transaction-local current-tenant setting, OR when the current role is the bypass role or inherits bypass membership while role inheritance is active; the naive membership-only form is forbidden because it leaked cross-tenant rows in an earlier table and was corrected by a forward migration. Superuser and inheriting administrative roles bypass RLS by design and are used only for migration, seed, and system-admin paths." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
