<urn:usf:delivery-facet:relationalstorageandmigrationsandrlsreadinessmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Readiness depends on the substrate being reachable and fully migrated; the migrated check (a non-empty migration ledger) and the cross-tenant isolation live-proof (an unfiltered count under a foreign tenant context returning zero) are the acceptance gates. When the substrate is unavailable the capability degrades explicitly, disabling mutation and side-effect paths while keeping read-only readiness and audit visible rather than failing silently. Promotion is blocked when readiness is unavailable or when the isolation or audit signal is missing." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
