<urn:usf:delivery-facet:relationalstorageandmigrationsandrlsstatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "State is held in a single canonical relational database with two tenant-isolation layers: a schema-per-tenant model where per-tenant configuration lives in tenant-scoped schemas selected by a transaction-local search path, and public-schema tenant-scoped tables carrying a tenant/organisation identifier column protected by row-level security. The migration ledger table tracks each applied file name (unique), its checksum, and apply timestamp; checksum is the first 16 hex characters of the SHA-256 of the committed file bytes, computed over the file with secret placeholders intact so it is identical across every environment. Tenant-scoped tables ENABLE and FORCE row-level security; provider substrates such as cache, search, and analytics are adapters behind ports and never own canonical schema." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
