<urn:usf:delivery-facet:relationalstorageandmigrationsandrlsvalidation> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The runner validates that every previously applied file still hashes to its recorded checksum on each run, refusing to advance on drift, and validates that the database has been migrated before any seed step executes. Identity and reference invariants are enforced in schema (uniqueness on natural keys, role and status check constraints, foreign keys), and the secret placeholder is validated by a trust-boundary check before materialisation. Tenant-identifier presence is a precondition for tenant-scoped access because RLS denies rows when the current-tenant setting is absent." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
