<urn:usf:delivery-facet:runtimesecretsmanagementauditmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "put, revoke, and delete emit audit-before-change records carrying only name, ref, and provider metadata and never the value, so the audit write precedes the store mutation. Where the use-case wraps the store write, an audit failure prevents the mutation, making audit a hard precondition for change. This guarantees a complete, value-free audit trail for every secret-lifecycle action." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
