<urn:usf:delivery-facet:runtimesecretsmanagementlifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The secret lifecycle is: put returns an opaque ref plus metadata, resolve returns the value only server-internally, rotate increments the version while keeping the same opaque ref, revoke disables resolution while retaining metadata, delete removes both metadata and the provider-held value, and readiness reports built-in and OpenBao backend health. A secret value is never returned by list or getMetadata; resolve is the single value-returning server path. Provider failure (OpenBao unreachable) reports degraded and never silently falls back to another backend." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
