<urn:usf:delivery-facet:runtimesecretsmanagementreadinessmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Readiness distinguishes built-in Postgres ready, OpenBao ready, and OpenBao degraded or unreachable, and emits secret-free readiness payloads; the built-in check is a Postgres SELECT 1 and the OpenBao check is its sys/health endpoint, and an OpenBao outage yields degraded rather than a fabricated ready. No silent fallback upgrades provider readiness, so a hermetic or composed state is never reported as a live-external-provider state." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
