<urn:usf:delivery-facet:runtimesecretsmanagementstatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "State comprises the secret ref, organisationId, name, provider in postgres|openbao, version, a revoked flag, the backend path, an encrypted_value for the built-in Postgres store or null when the value lives in OpenBao, and created, updated, and deleted metadata; list and getMetadata responses carry no value. The built-in store encrypts the value at rest while OpenBao holds the value entirely outside Postgres. Metadata is tenant-scoped under row-level security so refs do not leak across organisations." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
