<urn:usf:delivery-facet:scheduledjobsbuiltinontheeventsubstrateauditmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "scheduled_job.set and scheduled_job.run are audit-before-change operations, so the audit record is written before the schedule mutation or manual run takes effect. The recurring due-tick enqueue is represented operationally by the resulting platform_events records rather than as a separate user-mutation audit event. This keeps operator intent auditable while treating routine dispatch as operational telemetry." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
