<urn:usf:delivery-facet:scheduledjobsbuiltinontheeventsubstratelifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetKind> <urn:usf:facet-kind:lifecycle> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:scheduledjobsbuiltinontheeventsubstratelifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "An operator creates a schedule, the enabled job persists, a due tick enqueues a platform event, a same-window tick deduplicates so no duplicate event is enqueued, pausing disables due enqueue, run-now enqueues an event immediately, and an operator patch toggles the enabled flag. Scheduled dispatch is built directly on the event substrate, so an enqueued job becomes an ordinary platform_events record (for example a report.run event) carried by the durable-queue retry and dead-letter machinery. The daemon tick is invocable even though the continuous daemon loop is not claimed wired." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:delivery-facet:scheduledjobsbuiltinontheeventsubstratelifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementClass> "behavioural-runtime" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
