<urn:usf:delivery-facet:scheduledjobsbuiltinontheeventsubstrateproof> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Behaviour is exercised by two runtime proofs: scheduled-jobs validates live Postgres schedule persistence, due and run-now enqueue, row-level security, and the no-secret schema, and scheduled-job-routes validates the route handlers and access metadata, described in the corpus as level-4 live substrate and route validation. The proofs are the lineage evidence, not a USF readiness claim. Proof is hermetic/runtime lineage; fresh proof remains pending." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
