<urn:usf:delivery-facet:scheduledjobsbuiltinontheeventsubstratereadinessmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Readiness is that the due tick is invocable and the routes are accessible, even though the continuous daemon loop is not claimed; the live proof validates the table schema, row-level-security isolation, due/run-now enqueue behaviour, and the route handlers, and degrades explicitly when the substrate is unavailable. Because dispatch rides the event substrate, scheduled-job readiness inherits the event-bus degraded posture and never reports production-shaped behaviour as production-live." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
