<urn:usf:delivery-facet:scheduledjobsbuiltinontheeventsubstratestatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "State is the scheduled_jobs table holding organisationId, jobKey, eventType, intervalSeconds, an enabled flag, nextRunAt, and lastRunAt, together with an event idempotency window that prevents duplicate enqueue within the same due window. Enqueued jobs materialise as platform_events on the shared event substrate, so downstream state, ordering, retry, and dead-letter follow the event-bus state model. Row-level security scopes scheduled jobs to the owning organisation." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
