<urn:usf:delivery-facet:servicecatalogandproviderintegrationmodelcontracts> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The interface contract is the platform-services readiness surface and the service-catalog read API behind ports/adapters, returning catalog entries with their decision, visibility, entitlement, and readiness fields. Configuration is read from the declared provider/config plane and missing or invalid configuration fails closed rather than inventing UI defaults. Provider integration is mediated through ports so adapters can be swapped without changing the catalog contract." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
