<urn:usf:delivery-facet:servicecatalogandproviderintegrationmodelerrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Provider failure returns a typed degraded/readiness failure, keeps mutation boundaries closed, and does not fabricate successful provider state; degraded mode disables side-effecting paths that depend on the observability adapters while keeping read-only readiness and audit visible. Tenant data loss is possible only if migration, restore, or export semantics are bypassed, which the error model forbids. A missing tenant isolation or audit signal is an alertable tenant-data-or-security condition." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
