<urn:usf:delivery-facet:servicecatalogandproviderintegrationmodelpermissions> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Because it can affect tenant-visible data or access, it must preserve tenant isolation: visibility classifications (tenant_scoped_safe vs global_only vs not_exposed) and entitlement keys gate what each tenant can see and reach. Mutating operations are administrative and must keep mutation boundaries closed on failure. Tenant-scoped reads and clickthrough access are governed by the recorded visibility and entitlement model." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
