<urn:usf:delivery-facet:servicecatalogandproviderintegrationmodelstatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "State includes each service's key, name, and category; its environment model; visibility (tenant_scoped_safe, global_only, or not_exposed); the integration decision (build, compose, adapter, defer, or reject); the entitlement key; proof references; console-access flags; readiness status; and provider details. Database changes use ordered SQL migrations that must preserve this proven state model, and rollback is forward-fix or guarded restore after migration lineage is verified so tenant data is never silently dropped or remapped. As a tenant-data participant it is subject to tenant backup/export/retention/legal-hold semantics." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
