<urn:usf:delivery-facet:tenantdataimportexporterrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The model is fail-closed and explicitly designed so that failed transfers never silently lose data: a failed unit is recorded, completed units are preserved for resume, and provider (archive builder or applier) failure returns a typed degraded or readiness error with mutation boundaries closed. Tenant data cannot be silently dropped or remapped; incident class is tenant-data-or-security with explicit tenant-data-loss risk if export/import semantics are bypassed." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
