<urn:usf:delivery-facet:universalservicefoundationscopeandprinciplesauditmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Because it owns no tenant mutations its audit concern is the auditable governance record: changes to the foundation move through Git history, ADRs, and validator findings, which form the durable evidence trail. Readiness and audit signals remain visible even in degraded mode so the foundation's posture is always inspectable. Audit here is about preserving honest lineage of decisions, not row-level mutation logging." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
