<urn:usf:delivery-facet:universalservicefoundationscopeandprinciplescontracts> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The contract is normative rather than an HTTP surface (the V1 contract reference is n/a): it asserts the principles, authority order, and provability guarantees that bind every capability's interface and extraction. Configuration is read from the declared provider/config plane and missing or invalid configuration fails closed instead of inventing defaults. Conformant capabilities must preserve their proven lifecycle/readiness contract during extraction and keep mutation boundaries closed under failure." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
