<urn:usf:delivery-facet:universalservicefoundationscopeandprincipleserrormodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Failures fail closed: provider or dependency failure returns a typed degraded/readiness failure, mutation boundaries stay closed, and successful provider state is never fabricated. The principal risk is semantic drift or configuration loss rather than tenant data loss. Repeated typed errors past threshold, blocked readiness, or a failing promotion proof/smoke check are alertable foundation conditions." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
