<urn:usf:delivery-facet:universalservicefoundationscopeandprinciplesreadinessmodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "Readiness is the aggregate honesty of the foundation: a capability is ready only when its V1-proven contract, migration lineage, and proof inventory are intact and the matrix/registry/validation checks pass. Readiness fails closed when evidence is missing, stale, or unknown, and degraded mode keeps read-only readiness and audit visible. Promotion is gated on re-running the foundation matrix, registry, and validation after any fix." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
