<urn:usf:delivery-facet:universalservicefoundationscopeandprinciplesstatemodel> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "The state is the foundation asset graph itself: the capability inventory, the status vocabulary, V2 targets, completion actions, the path map, the proof inventory, the migration chain, package status, the service matrix, and validator findings. It holds no tenant data; its state is configuration- and evidence-shaped, so backup scope is configuration/evidence only and restore can never fabricate tenant records. State changes are governed by deliberate semantic decisions rather than runtime mutations." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
