<urn:usf:delivery-facet:workflowenginescheduledjobsapprovalslifecycle> <urn:usf:predicate:facetStatement> "A workflow starts into running, an approval.requested signal moves it to waiting, approval.granted completes it, approval.denied fails it, and an explicit cancel moves it to cancelled, with provider status read back through the orchestrator. Approval gates therefore drive deterministic state transitions and a denied approval fails the workflow rather than silently proceeding, while scheduled-job dispatch enqueues work onto the event substrate. Provider failure (Temporal or the in-memory orchestrator) degrades readiness and never falls back unsafely." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
