<urn:usf:implementation-conformance-rule:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:admissibilityRule> "A conformance test is admissible only when it imports the capability module at its graph-derived relative path, declares one subtest per outstanding applicable facet named exactly that facet canonicalName, and makes at least one assertion inside each such subtest against a value the module returned. A test that does not import the module, or that stubs it, evidences nothing and is refused before execution." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:implementation-conformance-rule:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:admissibleEvidenceClass> "implementation-conformance" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:implementation-conformance-rule:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:antiSelfWarrant> "The rule records what an execution returned. It never records satisfaction, and the facet evaluator remains the only authority that turns an outcome into a verdict." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:implementation-conformance-rule:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "v1" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:implementation-conformance-rule:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:conformanceCommand> "node --test --test-reporter=tap <conformance test path>" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:implementation-conformance-rule:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:coverageMode> "One behavioural test file per capability covering every outstanding applicable facet of that capability through subtests. Generating one test file per facet is prohibited: it is coverage theatre and it fragments behaviour that the module realizes together." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:implementation-conformance-rule:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:evidenceRule> "A facet is evidenced only by a subtest whose name equals the facet canonicalName, executed by the Node test runner against the real capability module, and reported by the runner as passing. A failing subtest is admissible evidence that the requirement is not met. An absent subtest is not evidence of anything." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:implementation-conformance-rule:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "A passing conformance outcome is evidence of observed module behaviour under test. It is not evidence of deployed product behaviour, integration behaviour or runtime composition." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:implementation-conformance-rule:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "An outcome records that a named behavioural test executed against the capability module and what each facet-named subtest returned. It does not claim the test is a complete characterization of the facet statement." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:implementation-conformance-rule:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:ImplementationConformanceRule> <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
