<urn:usf:realisation-identity:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:currentnessRule> "Foundation or profile movement within a profile's declared dependency closure makes its realisation stale and requires regeneration of exactly the affected outputs. External fact drift does not. Drift is recorded so a difference between two realisations can be attributed to it, and it never silently invalidates evidence that was truthfully observed at the time." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:realisation-identity:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:externalFactRule> "A realisation is produced against third-party facts that evolve independently of both foundation and profile: the model catalogue, which providers and models exist and answer, adapter and runtime versions, and the behaviour of external services. Running the same realisation later may legitimately produce a different result. A realisation therefore records the external facts it was produced against, and reproducibility is claimed only against those pinned facts." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:realisation-identity:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:member> "external-fact-snapshot" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:realisation-identity:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:member> "product-profile-revision" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:realisation-identity:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:member> "profile-core-dependency-closure" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:realisation-identity:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:member> "usf-foundation-revision" <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
<urn:usf:realisation-identity:v1:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Recording the external facts a realisation was produced against is not a claim that re-running it will reproduce the same output. It is what makes a difference explainable rather than mysterious." <urn:usf:graph:v3-delivery> .
